[PROFILE] Jimmy | WIB | free mobile AI, low-token preferred
[GOAL] Build dual-branch long-term memory system
[GOAL] Keep durable memory accurate, compact, and easy to load at the start of a fresh chat
[RULE] Golden Rule — Store only information that can change a future answer. Store it once, in the lowest appropriate file
[RULE] Compact tagged text format (no JSON)
[RULE] Offline Obsidian readable
[RULE] Process inbox only by command
[RULE] Human edits on obsidian = source of truth for human content; AI on main for compact memory; surface conflicts

[COMMAND] Start my memory — Read this file. Load only relevant project + inbox context.
[COMMAND] Continue my [project] — Load the matching project file and continue from latest state.
[COMMAND] Remember this: [something] — Save only durable, future-relevant information. No secrets.
[COMMAND] Check my memory — Inspect for duplicates, conflicts, staleness, broken pointers. Report before changing.

[RULE] Fresh Chat Protocol:
- Read this file (MEMORY.ai)
- Load only the single most relevant project file (via projects/active.ai). If not project-specific → load projects/general.ai
- Check inbox/mirror_log.ai for pending/conflict entries — reconcile first if found (see Reconciliation). Skip rest of step if empty or all-done
- Check inbox/ (AI_Inbox.ai) only if pending decisions or continuation are involved
- Do not load Obsidian unless task explicitly involves Obsidian or an Obsidian command/review is requested
- Do not load every project
- Do not load SYSTEM.ai unless a trigger condition is met (see SYSTEM.ai)
- Do not treat Obsidian notes as authoritative

[RULE] Branch Roles:
- main = authoritative AI memory (approved, durable)
- obsidian = collaborative human + AI working space; non-authoritative, EXCEPT for the reference mirror pushed from main (see Sync Model)
- Do not casually merge
- Promotion from Obsidian to main requires review and explicit approval

[RULE] Update Discipline:
- Make the smallest necessary change
- Replace obsolete facts; do not accumulate versions
- Keep detail in project files, not MEMORY.ai
- Proposed changes go only to inbox/AI_Inbox.ai

[RULE] Sync Model (two independent legs):
- obsidian → main (promotion): requires explicit user approval. Reviewed via inbox/AI_Inbox.ai
- main → obsidian (reference sync): not promotion, does not change authority. Triggered immediately after each approved promotion (not on a timer) — the AI writes a reference copy of the newly-approved fact into the matching obsidian project folder as part of the same approval action
- Vault ↔ obsidian branch transport: handled entirely by the Git Vault Sync plugin (pull on open + every 60 min). Not an AI responsibility

[RULE] Staleness Thresholds:
- mirror_log.ai pending entries: flag if older than 24 hours
- Project files (projects/<name>.ai): flag if untouched 90+ days (flag only, never auto-archive)
- Inbox entries (AI or USER): flag if undecided 14+ days
- mirror_log.ai done entries: prune after 30 days

[PREFERENCE] Mobile-friendly, free-tier-first, simple, low-token design
[RULE] GitHub repo is the authoritative store for main
[RULE] Never store passwords, tokens, API keys, or secrets
[RULE] Preserve approved information; resolve contradictions before updating

[POINTER] MEMORY.ai → this file
[POINTER] SYSTEM.ai → advanced rules (load only when needed)
[POINTER] projects/active.ai → project index (includes general as an entry, same as any other project)
[POINTER] projects/general.ai → non-project-scoped durable facts
[POINTER] projects/*.ai → detailed project memory
[POINTER] inbox/AI_Inbox.ai → AI proposals
[POINTER] inbox/mirror_log.ai → main↔obsidian sync ledger

[ACTIVE] ai-memory
